<h1>Points to Dollars Calculator</h1>
<p class="sub">Convert airline miles and credit card rewards into estimated cash value. Choose an illustrative valuation scenario or input your own custom CPP to model potential purchasing power.</p>

<div class="direct-answer">
  <strong>Direct Calculation Rule:</strong> Using a 1.5¢-per-mile illustrative airline-mile scenario, 50,000 miles represents roughly $750 in estimated travel value. This is a calculation example, not a live or guaranteed valuation for a specific loyalty program.
</div>

<div class="currency-selector" style="margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: right;"><button id="btnShare" class="btn-share">Share this calculation</button></div>
<div id="toast" class="toast">Link copied to clipboard!</div>

<div class="panel">
  <div class="field">
    <label for="totalPoints">Total points / miles in your account<span class="hint" id="hintTotal">Points</span></label>
    <input type="number" id="totalPoints" value="150000" min="0" step="1" inputmode="numeric" aria-describedby="hintTotal">
  </div>
  
  <div class="field">
    <label for="presetValuation">
      <span>Choose a valuation scenario (CPP)<button type="button" class="btn-help-toggle" id="btnHelpScenario" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="helpScenarioGuide">How do I choose?</button></span>
      <span class="hint" id="hintValuation">¢ / Point</span>
    </label>
    
    <div id="helpScenarioGuide" class="help-scenario-guide" style="display: none;">
      <h4>How to choose the right valuation scenario (CPP):</h4>
      <div class="guide-step">
        <strong>1. If you have a specific upcoming trip:</strong>
        <p>Calculate your actual CPP rather than using an illustrative preset: <code>Actual CPP = [(Cash Ticket Price - Award Taxes - Forgone Rewards) ÷ Points Required] × 100</code>.</p>
        <div class="guide-actions">
          <a href="/en/calculators/cents-per-point/" class="btn-link-action">Use CPP Calculator →</a>
          <a href="/en/calculators/points-vs-cash/" class="btn-link-action">Compare Points vs Cash →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-step">
        <strong>2. If you have past redemption history:</strong>
        <p>Use the median CPP across your last 3–5 similar redemptions to avoid skewing your portfolio with a single high-value anomaly.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-step">
        <strong>3. If you have no specific trip or history:</strong>
        <p>Start with the Conservative scenario (1.2¢), then test other presets to observe the range. Keep in mind: 0.6¢ does not apply to all hotel programs, 1.5¢ is not standard across all airlines, and 2.0¢ is never a guaranteed return.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <select id="presetValuation" aria-describedby="hintValuation unitValuation">
      <option value="custom">Custom CPP</option>
      <option value="0.6">Low-value points scenario: 0.6¢ per point</option>
      <option value="1.2">Conservative scenario: 1.2¢ per point</option>
      <option value="1.5" selected>Typical airline-mile scenario: 1.5¢ per point</option>
      <option value="2.0">Higher-value redemption scenario: 2.0¢ per point</option>
    </select>
    <input type="number" id="cppValue" value="1.5" min="0.01" step="0.01" style="margin-top:10px;" inputmode="decimal" aria-describedby="hintValuation unitValuation">
    <div class="unit" id="unitValuation">These CPP values are illustrative scenarios, not official conversion rates, live valuations, or guaranteed redemption values. The most reliable input comes from the cash price, taxes, fees, and points required for the redemption you are considering.</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="ticket" aria-live="polite">
  <div class="main">
    <div class="compare">
      <div class="item">
        <div class="k">Estimated Portfolio Value</div>
        <div class="v" id="dollarValue" style="word-break: break-word; overflow-wrap: anywhere;">$0</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="note" id="explain"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="callout" style="margin-top: 24px;">
  <strong>Core Consideration:</strong> Loyalty points carry no legal cash guarantee and face ongoing risk of program devaluation. A practical approach is to accumulate rewards for planned trips rather than hoarding large balances indefinitely.
</div>

<div class="article-content prose" style="margin-top: 40px;">
  <h2>Understanding Valuation Scenarios</h2>
